result.description:
For more than 39 years, companies have turned to Signs & Lines for award winning, creatively executed, quality signage.

Whilst signage has evolved significantly over time, the primary function remains the same – to convey a message. Combining years of experience, skilled craftsmanship and latest technologies, our talented team will craft your signs to ensure your message is seen.

Signs & Lines know signs … we love signs … we live and breathe signs – meaning your sign project is in safe hands.

We are seeking highly experienced SIGNWRITER to join our team of professionals on a full time and permanent basis.

MAIN RESPONSIBILITY:
To take a lead in the assembly and production output of the company producing signage to a high level of quality and professionalism.

Key Responsibilities & Skills:
Interpret detailed shop drawings and/or specifications to understand job, material and equipment requirements to produce acrylic, 3D fabricated signage, digital prints, vinyl application, LED placement and LED lightboxes.
Value engineer all works to maximise efficiency and reduce costs;
Assemble and make signage elements incorporating all signage types and styles to high quality with speed and accuracy.
Consistent production of dimensionally accurate signage elements through routine quality checks throughout the progress of production.
Take a lead role in sign making problem solving and raising any issues with management;
Maintain a high degree of attention to detail and follow company QMS requirements – complete relevant paperwork;
Maintain sufficient stock levels of materials and consumables, ordering items well in advance of signage works;
Ensure the assembly workshop and equipment is operating to safety standards, with high regard for risk and hazard management practices;
As and when there is a requirement, support and assist workflows in other areas of the business to keep production moving (may include site installation duties)
Compliance to OH&S and workplace/Worksafe safety issues;
Team player who offers assistance to colleagues and guidance to younger members of the team;
Good communicator – keeps all members of team in loop with progress & problems;
Independent and resourceful – solution (not problem) orientated;
Site works if required. To be able to solve problems on site and plan work on site to be done efficiently.
Any other reasonable duties.

If you meet the above criteria and would like to be considered for this position, please apply now!
Salary: Between $79,499 and $82,000 per annum + Super
